[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'AI agents are getting ridiculously good. They can browse the web, write code, send emails, update databases, and even automate entire workflows. But, there\'s one major problem. Would you actually trust an AI agent to do that all'

[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'completely on its own? Probably not. The reality is is that the best AI systems today don\'t give agents unlimited control. Instead, they combine predictable automation with AI reasoning'

[00:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and require human approval before anything important happens. In this video, I\'ll show you exactly how you can build that using Kestra. Kestra is an open-source workflow automation platform'

[00:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that lets you build and run automated workflows. Think of it as a way to orchestrate multiple tasks from APIs and databases to AI models in one reliable pipeline. We\'ll create an AI-powered'

[00:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'workflow that knows when to think, when to automate, and when to stop and ask for approval before taking action. Kestra is like an operating system for AI workflows. Cuz instead of letting an'

[01:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'AI agent run everything on its own, Kestra can manage the entire process with handling the predictable steps, calling AI only when reasoning is needed, and allowing a human to approve'

[01:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'important actions before anything happens. So, it is super simple and you can get started completely for free with the links in the description below. And I know you may be wondering, why not just use an AI? Well, because a'

[01:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'drag-and-drop canvas isn\'t just code. In Kestra, the whole workflow is a YAML file. You version it in Git, review it in a PR, deploy it through CI/CD, and roll it back when it breaks. You can run'

[01:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Python, Node, Go, and Bash natively inside a task instead of just wrapping everything in a custom node. And when something fails, you can get full execution history, replays, as well as'

